# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  Personal planning material — deliberately not published.
#
#  These directories hold the private 14-week schedule this work is executed
#  against. The public, technical version of the same roadmap lives in
#  docs/roadmap.md and is what belongs in a repository.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
plan/
archive/

# CLAUDE.md is working instructions for an assistant, not documentation of the
# system: local absolute paths, how to talk to me, what not to do for me. It
# belongs in the same category as plan/ — material this work is executed
# against rather than material it produces. What a reader needs is in
# RUNBOOK.md and docs/.
CLAUDE.md

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  Upstream source and build trees.
#
#  libspdm builds its own OpenSSL from a submodule: several GB, tens of
#  thousands of files, and none of it ours. What this repo carries instead is
#  third_party/*.pin — the exact commit hashes every result was produced from.
#  See docs/decisions/0001-two-build-flavors.md.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
third_party/*/
!third_party/*.pin
!third_party/README.md
lab/
work/
build/
*.o
*.a
*.so
*.exe

# c-drills: binaries are built from source by `make`, never committed.
c-drills/d[0-9]*
!c-drills/d[0-9]*.c
!c-drills/d[0-9]*.h
!c-drills/d[0-9]*.md

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Scratch / transient run output. Curated evidence under bench/data/ IS
# committed — that is the point of the project — but scratch runs are not.
bench/data/_scratch/
*.tmp
*.log
!docs/**/*.log

# ── the exception that had to be carved out, and why ─────────────────────────
#
# `*.log` above silently swallowed bench/data/*/‹arm›.req.log and .rsp.log.
# Those files are not build noise: they are the emulator stating what it parsed
# the flags as (`exe_conn - 0x0000001e`), which is the evidence behind more than
# one claim in LOG.md — and every one of them is listed, with a SHA-256, in the
# manifest.json committed beside it. So a fresh clone received a manifest
# attesting to four files that were not in the repository.
#
# That is the exact failure this project's provenance mechanism exists to make
# impossible, arriving through the one file nobody thinks of as a mechanism.
# The rule that follows: an ignore pattern is not allowed to outrank a
# manifest. `harness/verify_repo.sh` now checks that every artifact named in a
# manifest is actually tracked, so this cannot recur silently.
!bench/data/**/*.log

# Editor / OS
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Secrets. Nothing here should ever be committed, but make it explicit —
# W03 generates a private certificate chain and it is easy to be careless.
#
# It was. The first version of certs/gen_chain.sh also wrote
# end_responder.key.pem, and `*.key` does not match it, because a glob without
# a slash matches the END of a name. The rule looked like it covered the case
# and a private key sat one `git add` away from being published.
#
# Both spellings are listed now, and the real guarantee is not either of them:
# harness/verify_repo.sh reads every file git is tracking and refuses a PEM
# private-key header in any of them. A pattern says what someone expected to
# write; the grep says what is there.
*.key
*.key.pem
*.key.p8
!certs/**/*.key.example
id_ed25519*
*.pem.private
.env

# Intermediate certificate material. The CSRs and the curve parameters are
# reproducible from the certificates and carry nothing the chain does not.
certs/out/*.req
certs/out/param.pem
